{"name":"Jasper Park","hex":"#4a6558","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jasper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any bright-coloured kind of chalcedony apart from cornelian.","An opaque, impure variety of quartz, of red, yellow, and other dull colors, breaking conchoidally with a smooth surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with, or as if with, jasper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jasper"},{"term":"park","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of land set aside for environment preservation or recreation.","A tract of ground kept in its natural state, about or adjacent to a residence, such as for the preservation of game, for walking, riding, or the like."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bring (something such as a vehicle) to a halt or store in a specified place.","To defer (a matter) until a later date."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/park"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jasper National Park","blocks":[{"text":"Jasper National Park, in Alberta, Canada, is the largest national park within Alberta's Rocky Mountains, spanning 11,000 km2 (4,200 sq mi). It was established as Jasper Forest Park in 1907, renamed as a national park in 1930, and declared a UNESCO world heritage site in 1984. Its location is north of Banff National Park and west of Edmonton. The park contains the glaciers of the Columbia Icefield, springs, lakes, waterfalls and mountains."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Mount_Andromeda_at_dusk%2C_Jasper_National_Park%2C_Alberta%2C_Canada.jpg/330px-Mount_Andromeda_at_dusk%2C_Jasper_National_Park%2C_Alberta%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jasper_National_Park","wikidata":"Q503429"},{"title":"Jasper Park, Edmonton","blocks":[{"text":"Jasper Park is a neighbourhood in west Edmonton, Alberta, Canada that was once a part of the Town of Jasper Place. It became a part of Edmonton when Jasper Place amalgamated with Edmonton in 1964. It is a smaller residential neighbourhood bounded on the south by 87 Avenue, on the east by 149 Street, on the west by 156 Street, and on the north by 92 Avenue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/2007-09-24_Jasper_Park_023_Compressed.jpg/330px-2007-09-24_Jasper_Park_023_Compressed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jasper_Park%2C_Edmonton","wikidata":"Q6164021"},{"title":"Jasper","blocks":[{"text":"Jasper is an opaque type of silica that comes in a variety of colors, most commonly red, yellow, brown, green, and very rarely blue. It is made mostly of very fine-grained quartz or chalcedony, with other minerals contributing to its color and appearance. The common reddish color is due to iron inclusions. Jasper breaks with a smooth surface and is used for ornamentation or as a gemstone. It can be highly polished and is used for items such as vases, jewelry, seals, and snuff boxes. The density of jasper is typically 2.5 to 2.9 g/cm3. Jaspillite is a banded-iron-formation rock that often has distinctive bands of jasper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Jasper_outcrop_in_the_Bucegi_Mountains.jpg/330px-Jasper_outcrop_in_the_Bucegi_Mountains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jasper","wikidata":"Q201175"},{"title":"Park","blocks":[{"text":"A park is an area of natural, semi-natural or planted space set aside for human enjoyment and recreation or for the protection of wildlife or natural habitats. Urban parks are green spaces set aside for recreation inside towns and cities. National parks and country parks are green spaces used for recreation in the countryside. State parks and provincial parks are administered by sub-national government states and agencies. Parks may consist of grassy areas, rocks, soil and trees, but may also contain buildings and other artifacts such as monuments, fountains or playground structures. Many parks have fields for playing sports such as baseball and football, and paved areas for games such as basketball. Many parks have trails for walking, biking and other activities. Some parks are built adjacent to bodies of water or watercourses and may comprise a beach or boat dock area. Urban parks often have benches for sitting and may contain picnic tables and barbecue grills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Halleyparknovember_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Halleyparknovember_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park","wikidata":"Q22698"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Kane_Jasper_House.jpg/500px-Kane_Jasper_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Kane_Jasper_House.jpg/500px-Kane_Jasper_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paul Kane's sketch of Jasper House in November 1846.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKane_Jasper_House.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Jasper_Park_Information_Centre.jpg/500px-Jasper_Park_Information_Centre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Jasper_Park_Information_Centre.jpg/500px-Jasper_Park_Information_Centre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jasper Park Information Centre, originally constructed in 1914 as an administration building and as the park superintendent's residence","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJasper_Park_Information_Centre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Jasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg/500px-Jasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Jasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg/1280px-Jasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Jasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg/500px-Jasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"CNR advertisement, 1929","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJasper_Park_Lodge_%E2%80%94_Le_centre_du_plus_beau_complexe_de_loisirs_en_montagne_au_Canada_%E2%80%94_Canadien_National.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Jasper_Dwayne_Reilander-4.jpg/500px-Jasper_Dwayne_Reilander-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Jasper_Dwayne_Reilander-4.jpg/1280px-Jasper_Dwayne_Reilander-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Jasper_Dwayne_Reilander-4.jpg/500px-Jasper_Dwayne_Reilander-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"